  "$comment": "Dig & Discover tuning (everything configurable lives here). Distances in world units (1 block = 1 unit). materials: durability = the hand tool's hits, minPower = the digging power it takes (the blades' level gives it: digging), value = sell price per item, drops = items per block; block = the KayKit block model drawn for it, pickup = what flies into the backpack, decor = pieces poking out of the top. digging: the tractor's blades chew everything they and its body touch. A block takes chewSec seconds at just enough power, x falloff for each power over; shortSec[n - 1] when n powers short (more short = locked). zones: rings round the hub by distance (wobbly edges); fill = base rock, patches / ores = {id, chance}; height = how high its ground stands (ramps at the borders, zoneRamp wide); lava = {share, scale}: pools of it (slow to drive through: lava). tools: the pickaxe, then the tractors (vehicle): width = what they dig across, rideScale = their size, rideSpeed x walking speed, capacity = the bag they carry, tint = their colour. upgrades: the pads' repeatable tracks (blades: power; capacity: share more bag). bladeLevels: the blades drawn at each level. boosts: the HUD's POWER-UPS. levels: XP per level (next, then x growth), what gives it, the cash a level pays, the totem. finds, wardrobe, achievements, chests, richOre, prestige, mineThemes: see README.",
